r I like to just press  it in so it's easy to lift it out and  for just extra reassurance a quick  little spritz with some cooking spray  and we're going little spread  nails a fun farm take another banana  half of its for snacking half its for  decorating so just kind of cut it in  half take it out of its peel gets  challenging when I sew right you got any  delicate with it going to nestle this  down the center and we're going to  decorate with a few more of those  chocolate chips right on top so this is  going to go into a 350 degree oven for  about an hour  trust me it's worth it this is why we  have these little handles so easy look  how moist that looks oh my gosh so this  piece is all for me but there's still a  whole lot of love going on for my family  and if they want seconds they can make  it themselves when they get their  cookbook so let's have a little taste -  shall we mmm this is so good I still  have a few more recipes that I need to  create for my little cookbook for my  family and I'm going to be sharing  another one of my family's favorites in  an upcoming video so of course be sure  to subscribe so you don't miss out leave  me a comment below with some of your  family's favorite recipes and I'll see  you next time on Abbey's kitchen  you
 

